A43. The first thing you will do after getting the new car. ~ OWE
A44. What she said and then got into a pet. ~ NO
A45. What our neighbor's son scrapes off the violin every night. ~ SOLO
A47. The man who gets a run for his money (abbr.). ~ CR
A49. Like. ~ AS
A50. The way he found a taxi driver that rainy night in Newark. ~ RUDE
A52. No ingrowing affair is ever like this. ~ ENATE
A54. Talkie windups. ~ REELS
A56. What you had trouble finding in the income tax blanks. ~ SENSE
A58. A spotty thing to do. ~ PUT
A60. Their dippy jobs make these people change color easily. ~ DYERS
A63. The way he began trifling with the maid's affections. ~ TRI
A64. You're getting warm on this one. ~ TEPID
A66. This is lost in any great corporation. ~ LAP
A67. This may lead to two, then another and another— ~ ONE
A68. A German unit in the world war. ~ EIN
A69. To hang around the joints. ~ SAG
A71. Often preceded by the Christian. ~ ERA
A72. What he finally succeeded in putting round her neck. ~ PENDANT
