D12. What the night watchman sleeps by. ~ DAY
D14. What Washington was when he couldn't tell a lie. ~ LAD
D15. The head end backing up. ~ REAR
D22. Too much of these'll make you lazy. ~ EE
D25. International squabblers. ~ NATIONS
D26. The state a Swede finds himself in after landing at New York (abbr.). ~ SD
D28. XXXXXVVVVVVVVVVI. ~ CI
D29. To avoid girl friends love your wife this way. ~ UTTERLY
D31. What they'll probably do to Heflin if he keeps talking. ~ ELECT
D33. It's hardly safe for a nut like this to be in a fast-moving car. ~ LOOSE
D34. First name of a place with an option on wonderful climate. ~ LOS
D35. This is hell raising. ~ ADO
D39. His steno had to wait patiently after he said this. ~ AND
D40. American shocker. ~ POE
D46. Easy going. ~ LENIENT
